<title>JAPAN: Japan July imported vehicle sales fall 25.6% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan July imported vehicle sales fall 25.6% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales of imported vehicles in Japan fell 25.6 percent in July from a year earlier to 31,354 vehicles, the Japan Automobile Importers' Association (JAIA) said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of July sales, with percentage change from a year earlier:</p>
<p> Cars total		29,419  down  22.7 percent</p>
<p> - Cars over 2001 cc   19,446  down  29.9 percent</p>
<p> - Cars under 2000 cc   9,973  down   3.6 percent</p>
<p> Trucks total	     1,933  down  52.1 percent</p>
<p> - Heavy		    1,760  down  30.5 percent</p>
<p> - Light			173  down  88.5 percent</p>
<p> Buses			    2	    --</p>
<p>Exporting countries and selected makers' car sales in Japan</p>
<p>in July, with percentage changes from a year earlier:</p>
<p> German total		   14,077  down 18.1 percent</p>
<p>  Volkswagen Audi Group	5,359  down 11.0 percent</p>
<p>  -Volkswagen	 4,428  down 10.1 percent</p>
<p>  -Audi		   931  down 14.9 percent</p>
<p>  Adam Opel			2,619  down 24.9 percent</p>
<p>  BMW		   2,290  down 33.9 percent</p>
<p>  Mercedes-Benz     2,768  down  3.8 percent</p>
<p>  Ford-Werke AG	 749  down 30.3 percent</p>
<p>  Porsche		 274  up   12.8 percent</p>
<p> United States total	   8,506  down 34.3 percent</p>
<p>  Honda USA	   2,142  down 46.8 percent</p>
<p>  Ford Motor	     1,407  down 45.3 percent</p>
<p>  General Motors	2,554  up    1.0 percent</p>
<p>  Toyota		  435  down 79.0 percent</p>
<p>  Chrysler		 1,413  down 11.0 percent</p>
<p> Sweden total		    1,452  down 47.9 percent</p>
<p>  Volvo			    1,394  down 47.9 percent</p>
<p>  Saab				  58  down 48.7 percent</p>
<p> Britain total		   2,917  up   18.2 percent</p>
<p>  Rover group		    2,502  up   18.2 percent</p>
<p>  Jaguar			     188  down 28.2 percent</p>
<p>  Nissan		  169	 nil</p>
<p> France total			878  down 24.4 percent</p>
<p>  Peugeot Citroen    791  down 10.8 percent</p>
<p>  - Peugeot			  600  up    9.3 percent</p>
<p>  - Citroen			  191  down 43.5 percent</p>
<p>  Renault		 87  down 68.1 percent</p>
<p> Italy total			 746  up   25.8 percent</p>
<p>  Fiat group	    718  up   27.5 percent</p>
<p> Spain total			 207  down 70.9 percent</p>
<p>  Nissan			     207  down 70.9 percent</p>
<p> Netherlands			 452  vs  nil</p>
<p>  Mitsubishi	    452  vs  nil</p>
<p> Australia			   128  down 24.3 percent</p>
<p>  Mitsubishi			 128  down 24.3 percent</p>
<p>Note: General Motors' July car sales included 1,557 Cavaliers sold by Toyota. The July total included 13 Nissan AD vans made in Mexico, down 99.1 percent from a year before.</p>
<p>Of the total, sales of vehicles produced by overseas units of Japanese makers totalled 3,781 in July, down 55.6 percent from a year earlier.</p>
